course: dictionary
lesson: 9157
title: Words that sound like what they mean
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are named after the sound they make. Snort is one of them: say it out loud and you can almost hear a rough breath pushed out through the nose. Words like this help a reader picture a scene.
explain: Snort can be a verb or a noun. As a verb it is something you do: «The Rat only snorted and stayed outside.» The Rat did not join in, and his noisy breath showed he thought the idea was silly. As a noun it names the noise itself: «a snort».
explain: The clues around the word tell you why someone snorts. A laugh that bursts out suddenly, a scornful "Huh! As if!", or a horse clearing its nose can all be snorts. Read the whole sentence to find which one fits.
fact: To snort is to push air out loudly through your nose, making a rough sound.
fact: People snort when they laugh suddenly, or to show they do not believe or like something.
fact: Animals such as pigs and horses snort.
fact: A snort can also be the noise itself, as in «a snort».
fact: Snort is an onomatopoeia: a word that sounds like the noise it names.
exercise: «The Rat only snorted and stayed outside.» What does snorted show about the Rat? | *He did not like the idea and let out a rough, noisy breath | He had a cold and sneezed quietly | He was hungry and ate some bread | He was singing a happy tune
exercise: «Horses are flight animals that react first and think later, so they may snort and jump at a plastic bag.» What does snort mean here? | *To push air out loudly through the nose | To shake the saddle | To eat fast and loudly | To run away from the riders
exercise: Mice do not crawl up elephant trunks, because the trunk could blow anything out with a huge snort. Which creature's trunk could give the huge snort? | Rat | *Elephant | Mouse | Cat
test: In «a snort», what kind of word is snort? | *Noun | Adverb | Verb | Adjective
test: Why might a person snort? | To ask a polite question | To say hello to a friend | *To show they do not believe or like something | To tell the time
exam: What is an onomatopoeia, the kind of word snort is? | A long, quiet sigh | A type of bird | A kind of shoe | *A word that sounds like the noise it names
